{"book":"lines-angles","bookTitle":"Lines and angles","concept":7,"title":"Parallel lines and a transversal","grades":"Grade 8","goal":"I can use corresponding, alternate and co-interior angles on parallel lines.","teach":"A <b>transversal</b> cuts two parallel lines. <b>Corresponding</b> angles (same position at each crossing, an F shape) are equal. <b>Alternate</b> angles (on opposite sides, between the lines, a Z shape) are equal. <b>Co-interior</b> angles (same side, between the lines, a C shape) add up to 180°.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:403px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 309.8 215.6\"><g transform=\"translate(18.4,15.8)\"><line x1=\"15.6\" y1=\"46.8\" x2=\"257.4\" y2=\"46.8\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"15.6\" y1=\"136.5\" x2=\"257.4\" y2=\"136.5\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"97.5\" y1=\"6.2\" x2=\"191.1\" y2=\"177.8\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M111.5,31.9 A17,17 0 0 0 102.6,46.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"92.8\" y=\"35.4\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">a</text><path d=\"M160.4,121.6 A17,17 0 0 0 151.6,136.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"141.7\" y=\"125.1\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">a</text><path d=\"M127.8,61.7 A17,17 0 0 0 136.6,46.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"146.5\" y=\"67.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">b</text><path d=\"M185.6,136.5 A17,17 0 0 0 160.4,121.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"184.5\" y=\"114.2\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">c</text><path d=\"M130.5,51.8 L136.5,46.8 L130.5,41.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M130.5,141.5 L136.5,136.5 L130.5,131.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"3.6\" y=\"51.8\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A</text><text x=\"269.4\" y=\"51.8\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">B</text><text x=\"3.6\" y=\"141.5\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">C</text><text x=\"269.4\" y=\"141.5\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">D</text></g></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">Corresponding: a = a. Alternate: b and the top-left angle at H. Co-interior: b + c = 180°.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"AB ∥ CD. The angle at G below AB, on the right, is 65°. Find the angle at H above CD, on the right.","steps":["These angles are on the same side of the transversal, between the parallel lines: co-interior.","Co-interior angles add up to 180°.","The angle is 180° − 65° = 115°."]},"watch":"These rules work only when the lines are parallel. Look for the arrow marks (or ∥).<br><br><b>Problem-solving lens</b><br>Look for the letter shapes: F for corresponding, Z for alternate, C for co-interior.","qs":[{"text":"Find x.","vis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:403px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 309.8 215.6\"><g transform=\"translate(18.4,15.8)\"><line x1=\"15.6\" y1=\"46.8\" x2=\"257.4\" y2=\"46.8\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"15.6\" y1=\"136.5\" x2=\"257.4\" y2=\"136.5\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"97.5\" y1=\"6.2\" x2=\"191.1\" y2=\"177.8\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M127.8,61.7 A17,17 0 0 0 136.6,46.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" s